# Personal agent tooling. Stripped from the repo in #3 and kept out deliberately — it is
# local workflow scaffolding, not part of the product. Ignoring it (rather than merely
# deleting it) is what stops a stale checkout, or an agent branching from a pre-strip
# commit, from quietly re-committing the whole tree.
.claude/
.codex/
.agents/
.TerMinal/
.gitlab/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.status.md

